#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sciences - In brief" tvg-id="551232540" tvg-name="Vultures can spot a dead antelope from five kilometres away‚ while seals can dive into deep water‚ even under the ice. It is also said that many animals have a mysterious sixth sense: they can predict imminent natural disasters. Do animals access knowledge that is beyond humans? Are they cleverer than us?<br/>From 03.12.2023 07:50" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",42: The Answer to Almost Everything - Are Animals Cleverer than Us? (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (03.12.2023)
